[?2004hroot@c12379f96918:~/work# clear; cat > /task/output/analysis_notes.md <<'MD'
[?2004l[?2004h> # VAL-2 released analysis (SOP FG-017 rev. 4) - method notes and erratum background
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 1. Counting (`counts.tsv`, `qc.json`)
[?2004l[?2004h> Reads were counted for an sgRNA when the read carried that sgRNA's 20-nt spacer directly in front of
[?2004l[?2004h> the scaffold (`GTTTTAGAGCTA`), i.e. in the amplicon context given in the wet-lab notes
[?2004l[?2004h> (`...ACACCG [spacer] GTTTTAGAGCTAGAAATAG...`). Both orientations were accepted: run A (NextSeq, 1x75)
[?2004l[?2004h> reads are sense, run B (NovaSeq LIB15) reads are the reverse complement of the amplicon, which is why
[?2004l[?2004h> the hand-over script reported **0** reads for LIB15 (its `count_guides.py` only looks for the sense
[?2004l[?2004h> scaffold). With the orientation fix LIB15 yields 116805 mapped reads (90.3%), in line with the other
[?2004l[?2004h> libraries. All eight libraries of the sample sheet are counted and reported. Gene labels are from the
[?2004l[?2004h> current release (`library.tsv`, r2); the hand-over `counts_draft.tsv` still used the withdrawn release 1,
[?2004l[?2004h> in which 80 sgRNAs (20 genes) were mislabelled.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 2. Arm assignment - LIB10 and LIB15 are swapped in the submitted sample sheet
[?2004l[?2004h> The submitted sheet labels LIB10 as vehicle and LIB15 as drug. The libraries themselves say the
[?2004l[?2004h> opposite, and three independent lines of evidence agree:
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Reference genes.** Only the partition drug = {LIB10, LIB13, LIB14} vs vehicle = {LIB11, LIB12, LIB15}
[?2004l[?2004h>    reproduces the compound classes: the five known resistance genes go up and the five known
[?2004l[?2004h>    sensitisers go down by 1-2.7 log2 (signature gap 3.10 log2). Scanning all ten possible 3-vs-3
[?2004l[?2004h>    splits of the six day-14 libraries, every other split gives a gap of <= 0.99.
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Template dropouts.** The wet-lab notes state ~150 cells/sgRNA for the vehicle arm and only
[?2004l[?2004h>    ~25 cells/sgRNA for the drug arm, so the drug libraries must show Poisson zeros. LIB10, LIB13,
[?2004l[?2004h>    LIB14 have 13, 11, 12 sgRNAs with zero reads and count CV ~1.12-1.15, while LIB11, LIB12, LIB15
[?2004l[?2004h>    have 1, 0, 0 zeros and CV ~0.97. LIB10 therefore belongs to the drug arm, LIB15 to the vehicle arm.
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Replicate correlation.** In log space LIB15 correlates 0.954/0.955 with LIB11/LIB12 but only
[?2004l[?2004h>    0.83 with LIB10, so LIB15 is a genuine vehicle replicate (not a re-sequencing of a drug library).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> All reported quantities use the corrected arms (T0 = LIB8, LIB9; vehicle = LIB11, LIB12, LIB15;
[?2004l[?2004h> drug = LIB10, LIB13, LIB14); no library is dropped. This also fixes the hand-over analysis, which
[?2004l[?2004h> silently discarded LIB15 ("a library without reads is left out") and analysed 2 vehicle + 2 drug
[?2004l[?2004h> libraries.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 3. Gene table (`gene_summary.tsv`)
[?2004l[?2004h> Counts were depth-normalised by the mapped-read total of each library and log2 ratios were centred on
[?2004l[?2004h> the non-targeting guides so that the median non-targeting sgRNA is exactly 0 (SOP section 4).
[?2004l[?2004h> `lfc_fitness` = median over the gene's sgRNAs of log2(mean vehicle / mean T0);
[?2004l[?2004h> `lfc_drug` = median over the gene's sgRNAs of log2(mean drug / mean vehicle).
[?2004l[?2004h> Using median-of-ratios size factors instead changes nothing (max 0.017 log2). The scale behaves as
[?2004l[?2004h> the design predicts: 190 genes (the carried-forward fitness candidates) are depleted below -1 and the
[?2004l[?2004h> 40 putatively neutral genes sit within +-0.5.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Significance was taken from a count-aware negative-binomial model of the sgRNA abundances
[?2004l[?2004h> (MAGeCK `test`, treatment LIB10/13/14 vs control LIB11/12/15), because the drug arm is strongly
[?2004l[?2004h> under-templated and its rare guides have Poisson-dominated variance that a variance-homogeneous null
[?2004l[?2004h> over-calls. Gene p-values were taken in the observed direction and adjusted with Benjamini-Hochberg
[?2004l[?2004h> over the 230 genes; `drug_class` = sensitiser (FDR < 5%, depleted under drug), resistance
[?2004l[?2004h> (FDR < 5%, enriched under drug), else none. Result: 18 sensitisers, 18 resistance genes, 194 none.
[?2004l[?2004h> Validation on the reference genes: 10/10 established modifiers recovered with the expected class,
[?2004l[?2004h> 0/30 established neutral genes called. The FDR decision is not marginal - the largest FDR among the
[?2004l[?2004h> calls is 0.028, the smallest among the non-calls 0.066 - and all 36 calls move in the same direction
[?2004l[?2004h> in each of the three drug replicates. (A two-sided BH test gives the same list except TGT4571,
[?2004l[?2004h> FDR 0.057; TGT4571 is not on the mailed list, so the erratum is unaffected.)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 4. Erratum (`erratum.tsv`)
[?2004l[?2004h> Every gene of `handover/hits_mailed.tsv` is listed with a verdict (SOP section 5):
[?2004l[?2004h> `confirmed` where the released analysis classes the gene as sensitiser or resistance (26 genes),
[?2004l[?2004h> `retracted` where it is classified as none (14 genes). No reagent had been ordered on the mailed
[?2004l[?2004h> list, so the correction is editorial only. Two systematic faults in the mailed list:
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> * it was computed on the withdrawn release-1 gene labels, so 7 of the 14 retracted rows name a gene
[?2004l[?2004h>   that does not carry the sgRNAs that produced the statistic at all (TGT2478, TGT4232, TGT4662,
[?2004l[?2004h>   TGT3979 plus the shifted-partner labels TGT3362, TGT4344 ...); the sgRNAs involved now belong to
[?2004l[?2004h>   other genes, several of which are genuine modifiers under their correct r2 name;
[?2004l[?2004h> * it was computed without the drug replicate LIB15 (lost by the counting bug), and the hit list was
[?2004l[?2004h>   cut at "top 40 by |z|" with a 3-sigma rule instead of a 5% false discovery rate.
