[?2004l[?2004h> old=notes[notes.index('* it was computed on the withdrawn release-1 gene labels'):notes.index('  cut at "top 40 by |z|"')]
[?2004l[?2004h> new="""* it was computed on the withdrawn release-1 gene labels. Seven of the fourteen retracted rows name a
[?2004l[?2004h>   gene that does not carry the sgRNAs which produced the mailed statistic at all; those guide pools
[?2004l[?2004h>   belong, under release 2, to a different gene which *is* a modifier. The effect the colleague measured
[?2004l[?2004h>   was real but misattributed, and the name that was mailed has to be withdrawn:
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h>   | mailed (r1) name | verdict | r2 gene of the same 4 sgRNAs | released class |
[?2004l[?2004h>   |---|---|---|---|
[?2004l[?2004h>   | TGT4344 | retracted | TGT7853 | sensitiser |
[?2004l[?2004h>   | TGT0462 | retracted | TGT7971 | sensitiser |
[?2004l[?2004h>   | TGT3362 | retracted | TGT1631 | sensitiser |
[?2004l[?2004h>   | TGT2478 | retracted | TGT4168 | sensitiser |
[?2004l[?2004h>   | TGT4232 | retracted | TGT7793 | resistance |
[?2004l[?2004h>   | TGT4662 | retracted | TGT5795 | sensitiser |
[?2004l[?2004h>   | TGT3979 | retracted | TGT4331 | sensitiser |
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h>   The remaining seven retracted rows (TGT7728, TGT5816, TGT1012, TGT2987, TGT0409, TGT1378, TGT4120)
[?2004l[?2004h>   keep the correct name but are not modifiers at 5% FDR (their FDR is 0.49-0.84); their apparent
[?2004l[?2004h>   depletion/enrichment comes from the under-templated drug libraries (guides with 3-25 reads, see
[?2004l[?2004h>   e.g. TGT0409, whose only well-powered sgRNA does not change) and, for TGT1378/TGT3362-like rows,
[?2004l[?2004h>   from the mailed ranking, which was cut at "top 40 by |z|" with a 3-sigma rule instead of a 5% FDR.
[?2004l[?2004h> * the analysis behind the mailed list also dropped the drug replicate LIB15 (0 reads, counting bug),
[?2004l[?2004h>   so it compared 2 vehicle against 2 drug libraries and never used the re-sequenced library;
[?2004l[?2004h> * no confirmed row changes identity between releases (all four of its sgRNAs carry the same gene
[?2004l[?2004h>   label in r1 and r2), and every mailed gene is either confirmed with FDR <= 0.023 or retracted with
[?2004l[?2004h>   FDR >= 0.49 - there is no gene in the grey zone, so the erratum does not depend on the exact test.
[?2004l[?2004h> """
[?2004l[?2004h> open('/task/output/analysis_notes.md','w').write(notes.replace(old,new))
